{"name":"Supercalifragilisticexpialidocious","hex":"#ffff69","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"supercalifragilisticexpialidocious","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Fantastic, marvellous, wonderful."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/supercalifragilisticexpialidocious"}],"entries":[{"title":"Supercalifragilisticexpialidocious","blocks":[{"text":"\"Super­cali­fragilistic­expiali­docious\" is a song and single from the 1964 Disney musical film Mary Poppins. It was written by the Sherman Brothers, and sung by Julie Andrews and Dick Van Dyke. It also appears in the 2004 stage show version.\nBecause Mary Poppins was a period piece set in 1910, songs that sounded similar to songs of the period were wanted. The movie version finished at #36 in AFI's 100 Years...100 Songs survey of top tunes in American cinema."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/63/Supercalifradgilisticexpialidocious_by_Julie_Andrews_and_Dick_Van_Dyke_US_vinyl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supercalifragilisticexpialidocious"},{"title":"Supercalifragilisticexpialidocious (collection)","blocks":[{"text":"Supercalifragilisticexpialidocious, sometimes shortened to Supercalifragilistic, is the twentieth collection by British designer Alexander McQueen, released for the Autumn/Winter 2002 season of his eponymous fashion house. Its title comes from the Mary Poppins song \"Supercalifragilisticexpialidocious\" (1964). Supercalifragilistic was primarily inspired by the Gothic aesthetic of American director Tim Burton, as well as fairy tales, English school uniforms, and the history of the French Revolution. The collection was heavily sexualised with concepts from fetish fashion such as leather harnesses and sexualised school uniforms. Historicist elements were drawn from the French queen Marie Antoinette, known for her interest in fashion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Parachute_Cape_by_Alexander_McQueen%2C_Savage_Beauty_exhibition.jpg/330px-Parachute_Cape_by_Alexander_McQueen%2C_Savage_Beauty_exhibition.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supercalifragilisticexpialidocious_(collection)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Lee_Alexander_McQueen_%26_Ann_Ray_-_Rendez-Vous_55.jpg/500px-Lee_Alexander_McQueen_%26_Ann_Ray_-_Rendez-Vous_55.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Lee_Alexander_McQueen_%26_Ann_Ray_-_Rendez-Vous_55.jpg/1280px-Lee_Alexander_McQueen_%26_Ann_Ray_-_Rendez-Vous_55.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Lee_Alexander_McQueen_%26_Ann_Ray_-_Rendez-Vous_55.jpg/500px-Lee_Alexander_McQueen_%26_Ann_Ray_-_Rendez-Vous_55.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Little black dress from the collection at Lee Alexander McQueen & Ann Ray - Rendez-Vous (2024)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALee_Alexander_McQueen_%26_Ann_Ray_-_Rendez-Vous_55.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/House_of_McQueen_exhibition_2025_74.jpg/500px-House_of_McQueen_exhibition_2025_74.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/House_of_McQueen_exhibition_2025_74.jpg/1280px-House_of_McQueen_exhibition_2025_74.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/House_of_McQueen_exhibition_2025_74.jpg/500px-House_of_McQueen_exhibition_2025_74.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"S